O6SJc60aMxW","user":{"login":"ColinSORourke","id":44822820,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0ODIyODIw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44822820?u=a3ed7540f46720cbf73f01b590fd1ef225d39344&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke","html_url":"https://github.com/ColinSORourke","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105701#pullrequestreview-3026766934","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/105701","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105701#pullrequestreview-3026766934"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/105701"}},"submitted_at":"2025-07-16T20:25:40Z","commit_id":null},{"id":3094488756,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc64cia0","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?u=68d23e7ee9cdf810da125e8510b72f845b9dccc8&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Tested locally, it works as expected on Compatibility. This is a great start, but I think we can push further on usability, especially for less programmer-centric workflows such as VFX.\r\n\r\n**Testing project:** [test_pr_105701.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/21640832/test_pr_105701.zip)\r\n*Press <kbd>K</kbd> to toggle real-time texture updates to compare performance.*\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4d721cad-a0e9-4065-81c2-24d00f8ce6c0\r\n\r\n*Original shader: [Colorful Bubbles](https://www.shadertoy.com/view/4d3BWH) by JuliaPoo*\r\n\r\nSome feedback:\r\n\r\n- It currently doesn't work on Forward+/Mobile, but this is expected given what's said in OP.\r\n- It took me a long time to figure out how you associate the shader with the DrawableTexture resource. I originally expected there would be a ShaderrMaterial property on the DrawableTexture, where you could assign a material (with its uniforms) and its shader.\r\n  - The width/height, format and mipmaps could be set directly as properties on the DrawableTexture inspector. Combine this with a property to set an array of base textures and a ShaderMaterial, and you wouldn't need any script for basic usage. More advanced usage (e.g. blitting over an area that isn't the whole texture size) would still warrant a script, but the use case for creating procedural textures would be simplified a lot.\r\n\r\n  - I think we can provide this high-level functionality and keep low-level behavior intact, but we need to make sure it's not initializing textures twice in this case (e.g. by reading inspector properties then the user's own `start()` call).\r\n\r\n  - Additionally, there is no quick way to just use a plain background color to blit over the entire area to apply your own shader. Some procedural textures initialize/update asynchronously, so using GradientTexture2D won't work unless you `await get_tree().process_frame`, which is not possible if you attach the script directly to the DrawableTexture2D like I originally did (since it's a Resource and can't access SceneTree directly). I ended up attaching the script to a node instead so I could use `_process()`, but I figured it was worth mentioning nonetheless. The testing project also includes a pure black `black.png` image for this purpose.\r\n\r\n- Having a DrawableTexture already set on a material property won't update it if you call `start()` to initialize it. You need to set it in a script again after calling `start()` for it to be recognized:\r\n\r\n```gdscript\r\n\tdrawable_texture.setup(64, 64, DrawableTexture2D.DRAWABLE_FORMAT_RGBA8, true)\r\n\tdrawable_texture.blit_rect(Rect2(0, 0, 64, 64), preload(\"res://white.png\"), Color.WHITE, 0, preload(\"res://drawable_texture_material.tres\"))\r\n\tmaterial_override.albedo_texture = drawable_texture  # This line is required for the texture to appear, even if we loaded it in the inspector previously.\r\n```\r\n\r\nIf you update the texture in real-time, you also need the last line to be in `_process()`, which is more resource-intensive than it could be.\r\n\r\n- Passing `null` as a texture parameter in `blit_rect()` causes a crash:\r\n\r\n```\r\nhandle_crash: Program crashed with signal 11\r\nEngine version: Godot Engine v4.5.beta.custom_build (faf3a2d29b8775eb2354e339d353b03869041aa0)\r\nDumping the backtrace. Please include this when reporting the bug on: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues\r\n[1] /lib64/libc.so.6(+0x19c30) [0x7f3859827c30] (??:0)\r\n[2] /home/hugo/Documents/Git/godotengine/godot/bin/godot.linuxbsd.editor.x86_64() [0x8d917b4] (/home/hugo/Documents/Git/godotengine/godot/scene/resources/drawable_texture_2d.cpp:98 (discriminator 1))\r\n[3] /home/hugo/Documents/Git/godotengine/godot/bin/godot.linuxbsd.editor.x86_64() [0x8f7fda6] (/home/hugo/Documents/Git/godotengine/godot/core/variant/binder_common.h:223 (discriminator 9))\r\n[4] /home/hugo/Documents/Git/godotengine/godot/bin/godot.linuxbsd.editor.x86_64() [0x8f58f99] (/home/hugo/Documents/Git/godotengine/godot/core/variant/binder_common.h:371)\r\n[5] /home/hugo/Documents/Git/godotengine/godot/bin/godot.linuxbsd.editor.x86_64() [0x8f38610] (/home/hugo/Documents/Git/godotengine/godot/core/object/method_bind.h:337 (discriminator 1))\r\n[6] /home/hugo/Documents/Git/godotengine/godot/bin/godot.linuxbsd.editor.x86_64() [0x47e7288] (/home/hugo/Documents/Git/godotengine/godot/modules/gdscript/gdscript_vm.cpp:2054 (discriminator 1))\r\n[7] /home/hugo/Documents/Git/godotengine/godot/bin/godot.linuxbsd.editor.x86_64() [0x4574442] (/home/hugo/Documents/Git/godotengine/godot/modules/gdscript/gdscript.cpp:192)\r\n[8] /home/hugo/Documents/Git/godotengine/godot/bin/godot.linuxbsd.editor.x86_64() [0x4575e88] (/home/hugo/Documents/Git/godotengine/godot/modules/gdscript/gdscript.cpp:425)\r\n[9] /home/hugo/Documents/Git/godotengine/godot/bin/godot.linuxbsd.editor.x86_64() [0xb2ac980] (/home/hugo/Documents/Git/godotengine/godot/core/object/object.cpp:1019 (discriminator 2))\r\n[10] /home/hugo/Documents/Git/godotengine/godot/bin/godot.linuxbsd.editor.x86_64() [0xb2a8730] (/home/hugo/Documents/Git/godotengine/godot/core/object/object.cpp:314)\r\n[11] /home/hugo/Documents/Git/godotengine/godot/bin/godot.linuxbsd.editor.x86_64() [0x90c3ec4] (/home/hugo/Documents/Git/godotengine/godot/core/string/string_name.h:182)\r\n[12] /home/hugo/Documents/Git/godotengine/godot/bin/godot.linuxbsd.editor.x86_64() [0x90c837b] (/home/hugo/Documents/Git/godotengine/godot/scene/resources/resource_format_text.cpp:1412 (discriminator 1))\r\n[13] /home/hugo/Documents/Git/godotengine/godot/bin/godot.linuxbsd.editor.x86_64() [0xab91a4f] (/home/hugo/Documents/Git/godotengine/godot/core/io/resource_loader.cpp:314 (discriminator 1))\r\n[14] /home/hugo/Documents/Git/godotengine/godot/bin/godot.linuxbsd.editor.x86_64() [0xab92604] (/home/hugo/Documents/Git/godotengine/godot/core/io/resource_loader.cpp:396 (discriminator 7))\r\n[15] /home/hugo/Documents/Git/godotengine/godot/bin/godot.linuxbsd.editor.x86_64() [0xab93675] (/home/hugo/Documents/Git/godotengine/godot/core/io/resource_loader.cpp:663)\r\n[16] /home/hugo/Documents/Git/godotengine/godot/bin/godot.linuxbsd.editor.x86_64() [0x90c14f6] (/home/hugo/Documents/Git/godotengine/godot/scene/resources/resource_format_text.cpp:463 (discriminator 5))\r\n[17] /home/hugo/Documents/Git/godotengine/godot/bin/godot.linuxbsd.editor.x86_64() [0x90c837b] (/home/hugo/Documents/Git/godotengine/godot/scene/resources/resource_format_text.cpp:1412 (discriminator 1))\r\n[18] /home/hugo/Documents/Git/godotengine/godot/bin/godot.linuxbsd.editor.x86_64() [0xab91a4f] (/home/hugo/Documents/Git/godotengine/godot/core/io/resource_loader.cpp:314 (discriminator 1))\r\n[19] /home/hugo/Documents/Git/godotengine/godot/bin/godot.linuxbsd.editor.x86_64() [0xab92604] (/home/hugo/Documents/Git/godotengine/godot/core/io/resource_loader.cpp:396 (discriminator 7))\r\n[20] /home/hugo/Documents/Git/godotengine/godot/bin/godot.linuxbsd.editor.x86_64() [0xab93675] (/home/hugo/Documents/Git/godotengine/godot/core/io/resource_loader.cpp:663)\r\n[21] /home/hugo/Documents/Git/godotengine/godot/bin/godot.linuxbsd.editor.x86_64() [0xab92f95] (/home/hugo/Documents/Git/godotengine/godot/core/io/resource_loader.cpp:555)\r\n[22] /home/hugo/Documents/Git/godotengine/godot/bin/godot.linuxbsd.editor.x86_64() [0x3caab3a] (/home/hugo/Documents/Git/godotengine/godot/main/main.cpp:4555 (discriminator 1))\r\n[23] /home/hugo/Documents/Git/godotengine/godot/bin/godot.linuxbsd.editor.x86_64() [0x3ba3299] (/home/hugo/Documents/Git/godotengine/godot/platform/linuxbsd/godot_linuxbsd.cpp:84 (discriminator 1))\r\n[24] /lib64/libc.so.6(+0x35f5) [0x7f38598115f5] (??:0)\r\n[25] /lib64/libc.so.6(__libc_start_main+0x88) [0x7f38598116a8] (??:0)\r\n[26] /home/hugo/Documents/Git/godotengine/godot/bin/godot.linuxbsd.editor.x86_64() [0x3ba30a5] (??:?)\r\n-- END OF C++ BACKTRACE --\r\n```\r\n\r\n- `COLOR` builtins are named `COLOR`/`COLOR2`/`COLOR3`/`COLOR4`, but sky shaders go for different numbering as per the [documentation](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/sky_shader.html#global-built-ins):\r\n\r\n> There are 4 `LIGHTX` lights, accessed as `LIGHT0`, `LIGHT1`, `LIGHT2`, and `LIGHT3`.\r\n\r\nI'd go for `COLOR0`/`COLOR1`/`COLOR2`/`COLOR3` for consistency.\r\n\r\n- DrawableTexture should get its own icon, so it can look different from Texture2D (which is an abstract class, and therefore has a gray icon):\r\n\r\n<img width=\"279\" height=\"573\" alt=\"Screenshot_20250806_225450\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8564759a-6b6f-484f-a99d-3169f2cb1b61\" />\r\n\r\nFor future PRs:\r\n\r\n- `TIME` is not accessible in `texture_blit` shaders, but I think it should to make procedural effects easier. You can emulate it for now by passing a `time` uniform manually in `_process()`, then calling `setup()` every frame.\r\n\r\n  - Having this as a built-in implementation would also need an update mode property in DrawableTexture, which would control when to update the texture: **Automatic** (always update only if `TIME` is used), **Once**, **Always**.","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105701#pullrequestreview-3094488756","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/105701","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105701#pullrequestreview-3094488756"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/105701"}},"submitted_at":"2025-08-06T22:19:57Z","commit_id":null},{"id":3115838485,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc65t-wV","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?u=68d23e7ee9cdf810da125e8510b72f845b9dccc8&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105701#pullrequestreview-3115838485","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/105701","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105701#pullrequestreview-3115838485"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/105701"}},"submitted_at":"2025-08-13T12:41:12Z","commit_id":null},{"id":3117870864,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc651u8Q","user":{"login":"ColinSORourke","id":44822820,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0ODIyODIw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44822820?u=a3ed7540f46720cbf73f01b590fd1ef225d39344&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke","html_url":"https://github.com/ColinSORourke","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105701#pullrequestreview-3117870864","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/105701","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105701#pullrequestreview-3117870864"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/105701"}},"submitted_at":"2025-08-13T22:12:27Z","commit_id":null},{"id":3256346196,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7CF-ZU","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?u=96b5dc9be2859dca5f31314c87d99a68a21e1576&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"@ColinSORourke @clayjohn OK, code wise I think this all looks good, nothing stands out to me that needs touching up. The only thing really is that the `linear_to_srgb` conversion is an all or nothing deal. In the sample project that I made it's important that only SOURCE0 is converted. However by setting the correct format I think it worked correctly anyway.\r\n\r\nSo I created a sample project, a very bare bones texture painter that paints albedo/normal/ao/roughness and metallic. It all worked very well and did exactly what it should do.\r\nYou can find the resulting demo project here: https://github.com/BastiaanOlij/drawable-textures-demo\r\n\r\nI also streamed developing this, it's a 2 hour watch but might help provide some more context: https://www.youtube.com/live/O1gwSoXTv_g\r\n\r\nThere is room for improvement but the things I ran into can all be follow up things, the heart of this is solid and I'm for merging the implementation as is.\r\nThe things I think we should consider for the future are:\r\n- I missed the ability to set a default color for the content. White is not a good default for a normal map or ORM texture :)\r\n- I know Reduz was adamant around the `setup` function and doing everything in code, but working with it I feel it makes far more sense to make these properties of the texture.\r\n- The aforementioned issues with wanting more control/certainty about linear output v.s. sRGB output.","state":"APPROVED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105701#pullrequestreview-3256346196","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/105701","author_association":"CONTRIBUT